      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "**Staged two-run repair workflow.**\n\nRun this graph first. It samples 1344x768 H3 and saves the nested video/audio\nlatent as `h3/q4-1344-latent_00001.h3latent.pt`.\n\nThen run `03-h3-staged-video-audio-decode.json` separately. Keeping sampling\nand VAE decode in different ComfyUI runs prevents the NestedTensor SaveLatent\ncrash and keeps peak memory bounded.\n\nThe custom `SaveH3StagedLatent` node stores the two nested tensors separately;\ndo not replace it with the stock `SaveLatent` node."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1440,
        570
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        400
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 14,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Turbo LoRA",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## 4-step Turbo LoRA\n\nSampling runs in 4 steps instead of 20.\n\n**Leave `low_vram` ON.** It is not a memory setting despite the name: on, the LoRA\ndelta is folded into the weights once at load; off, it applies as a hook on every\npass. On a quantised base the folded path is the one that keeps skin clean.\n\n**The custom sampler is required.** Video and audio inside H3 follow two different\nflow schedules. A stock sampler oversteps the audio at 4 steps and breaks it.\n\n**Close-up faces are this LoRA's weak point.** These are preview weights and skin\ncan go plastic at close range. For close-ups, bypass the LoRA node (Ctrl+B), set\nsteps to 20, and swap the sampler input to a KSamplerSelect."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
